==================================================
IMPORTANT: DO NOT OVERENGINEER
==================================================

This is extremely important.

Do NOT turn a simple exam question into a professional software architecture.

Do NOT create:

- 10 helper functions for a 5-line problem
- unnecessary classes
- unnecessary configuration objects
- unnecessary abstraction
- unnecessary validation
- unnecessary comments
- unnecessary error-handling frameworks

Prefer obvious code.

Example:

If I ask you to create a paragraph dynamically, I want something like:

var p = document.createElement("p");
var text = document.createTextNode("Hello");
p.appendChild(text);
document.getElementById("output").appendChild(p);

NOT a complicated DOM utility library.

